    "chunk_size_bytes": 1416,
    "chunk_text": "Then, I would like to speak about the late Hon. Gamini Lokuge, whose two daughters and family I know. I was not in Sri Lanka when he passed away. I would like to say that he was also a part of the 1977 group of late President J. R. Jayewardene. When the UNP was transitioning from a right-wing party to a centre-right party under President J.R. Jayewardene, for the first ever time, the UNP formed a trade union: the Jathika Sevaka Sangamaya. The Hon. Gamini Lokuge was one of the key people who were involved with late President J.R. Jayewardene in forming the Jathika Sevaka Sangamaya. He spent a lot of time in it on behalf of the workers. He was a fighter and served the party and the country, holding many portfolios subsequently. He had been a Member of the United National Party, I think, since 1960; he had also been a very senior Working Committee Member of that party. I extend my sympathies to his family.\n\nThen, I would like to speak about the late Hon. W.B. Ranatunga, who was from the Kotmale Seat. He entered Parliament in 1989 under late President R. Premadasa. The Hon. W.B. Ranatunga worked with me when I was the Chairman and subsequently, the General Secretary of the United National Party. We worked together for quite a while. He was a very amiable person; he was too good for politics being a very kind, quiet person, but still, he served and did his job. I extend my sympathies to his family."
