    "chunk_size_bytes": 1617,
    "chunk_text": "Madam, I would like to point out that I had referred this issue to the Committee on Public Finance chaired by the Hon. (Dr.) Harsha de Silva. That whole episode was inquired into by the Committee led by him and he submitted a report. That 600-page report mentioned very clearly that the Auditor-General must submit a forensic audit on the loss that was to be incurred to the Government as a result of this dubious contract to be given to a very dubious company registered in Dubai and which was also using a company like the VFS as a front to do it. I do not know why the VFS got into such a very dubious contract. However, being a reputed company, they themselves had got their names also tarnished in the process. Anyway, the main matter is up for argument on the 20th of November, and we are yet to receive the forensic audit report by the Auditor-General. Therefore, I want to put it on record here so that he would expeditiously make it available and it would be available for us, the petitioners, to be brought to the notice of the court when the matter is taken up for argument.\n\nBeyond that, I would like to talk about some of the disasters that we faced recently, particularly the frequent floods that we experienced in Akurana area. We had requested the District Development Committee to involve the Sri Lanka Land Reclamation and Development Corporation to address that particular issue. But, so far, no concrete decision has been made except to take action against unauthorized structures which are causing flooding of the Akurana Town. We are now facing the\n\n827 828\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dca\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0"
