    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0ddd\u0dba \u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dba\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dba\u0dcf \u0daf\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf, \u0ddd\u0da9\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dbd\u0dca\u0da9\u0dca \u0da7\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dca\u0db4\u0dca\u0db4 \u0d89\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0dbb \u0ddd\u0dca\u0db4 \u0dbb \u0dc0\u0dbd\u0dca \u0dc4 \u0dad\u0db8\u0dba\u0dba\u0dd2 \u0dd2 \u0dba\u0dba 20 tax \u0d91\u0d9a \u0daf\u0dd3\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0dad\u0dd2\u0ddd\u0db6\u0db1\u0dca\u0ddd\u0db1\u0dca \u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dba\u0db1 \u0d91\u0d9a.\n\n\uf0b7 Erosion of trust: Abrupt and untested policy shifts\n\ndamage Sri Lanka\u2019s investment climate, discouraging both local and foreign investment.\n\n\uf0b7 Sectoral vulnerabilities:\n\nWith regard to the tea industry, Mr. Karunaratne said that there would be cash delays cascading to smallholders and factories. Then, for rubber, Mr. Janadheera mentioned that high-value inputs would be blocked, undermining competitiveness. Mr. Marikar was of the view that many SMEs and diversified exporters are facing existential collapse while with regard to logistics and shipping, Mr. Van Dort pointed out that the entire ecosystem has been weakened, eroding Sri Lanka's role as a hub. Deemed exporters were not represented, but they are one of the biggest sectors in this SVAT refund mechanism.\n\nSir, while the Government justifies the decision on the grounds of curbing fraud and revenue leakage, industrial leaders stress that targeted audits, digital monitoring and strict penalties would have been sufficient. Instead, a blanket policy has \"carpet-bombed\" exporters, delivering no real revenue, but only a cash flow advantage to the Treasury at the expense of those who earn vital foreign exchange.\n\nSir, at a time when Sri Lanka must raise export earnings from US Dollars 16 to 17 billion in 2024 to US Dollars 36 billion by 2030, as pledged by President Anura\n\nKumara Dissanayake, this policy risks becoming a self-inflicted wound on our most crucial economic sector.\n\nTherefore, the Question I ask from the Hon. Minister of Finance is as follows:\n\n1. Will the Hon. Minister state what immediate remedial measures are being implemented to prevent refund delays spanning minimum 105 days or more, which are creating a crippling cash flow crisis, particularly for small and medium enterprises borrowing at double-digit interest rates?"
