    "chunk_text": "\u0b9a\u0bb5\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bcd: \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf, \u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb0 \u0b85\u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bcd \u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd\n\n\u0b85\u0b95\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0ba4\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc2\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1 CHALLENGE OF MEETING OFFICIAL RESERVE\n\nASSETS TARGET: STATEMENT BY ACTING\n\nMINISTER OF FINANCE, PLANNING AND\n\nECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT\n\nUS Dollars 7.2 billion of Gross Official Reserves by the end of December, 2025 is the IMF projection for Sri Lanka. Under the IMF-EFF Programme, achieving that Gross Official Reserves level is not considered a quantitative or a continuous performance criterion. The applicable target related to reserves build-up under the IMF-EFF Programme is the Net International Reserves -\n\n891 892\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dba\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dc4\u0dd0\u0dca\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd0\u0dca\u0db4\u0db6\u0dca\u0dae 24\n\nNIR. Net International Reserves is the difference between the Gross Official Reserves and the reserve-related liabilities, subject to some adjustments as per the Technical Memorandum of Understanding. So, that is the net position, in a way. The NIR target achievement by end June and end December of each year is monitored at the corresponding reviews. Sri Lanka has already achieved the end December, 2024 NIR target comfortably through substantial net purchases of foreign exchange from the domestic foreign exchange market. Based on the current level of net purchases, Sri Lanka is in line to achieve the end June and end December, 2025 Net International Reserves targets.\n\nAccordingly, the Answers to the specific questions raised are as follows:\n\n1. US Dollars 7.2 billion is the projection of the IMF and is not a compulsion under the IMF -EFF Programme. By end August, 2025, the Central Bank had absorbed more than US Dollars 1.2 billion from the domestic forex market to build up Gross Official Reserves and the Central Bank will continue to monitor and implement necessary mechanisms to meet the requirements."
