    "chunk_text": "country and not what is good for the independent Central Bank, which buys cars they want and increases salaries as they want while the rest of the country does not get those benefits.\n\nThank you, Sir.\n\nFor example, if we take the export income, as of August, it had exceeded US Dollars 11 billion. In the mean time, the foreign exchange earnings, remittances and earnings from tourism have also been robust. - [Interruption.] Yes, that is true. But, of course, we need to allow the Central Bank to function and respect them because it operates with its own autonomy. The actions taken by the Central Bank in the past in maintaining the required levels as well as last year with regard to acquisition of foreign exchange have been all right. I just explained to you about the current position. We have more time to achieve the targets and during that time, they would use their tools appropriately.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Minister, with Net Reserves being US Dollars 6.186 billion, the IMF fifth tranche amounting to US Dollars 330 million coming in and I am informed that there would also be an ADB funding of US Dollars 190 million, you will have roughly about US Dollars 6.7 billion. But, what about the balance of that US Dollars 7.2 billion target? You all should achieve that also. Otherwise, macro-linked bond holders would look at whether to move out or come in, and that would have an impact on the valuation of the rupee. That is the reason why I am pushing for this. Every 1 per cent depreciation of the rupee has an impact of Rs. 46 billion on Government\u2019s expenditure. That is the concern. One per cent interest rate has an impact of Rs.160 billion on the economy. So, Hon. Minister, we do not need to tell you these things because you have practical knowledge. Therefore, what I am saying is, together, we must ensure that the economy does not get stymied or get caught to the bureaucratic forces who are out there."
  },
