    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Minister, with Net Reserves being US Dollars 6.186 billion, the IMF fifth tranche amounting to US Dollars 330 million coming in and I am informed that there would also be an ADB funding of US Dollars 190 million, you will have roughly about US Dollars 6.7 billion. But, what about the balance of that US Dollars 7.2 billion target? You all should achieve that also. Otherwise, macro-linked bond holders would look at whether to move out or come in, and that would have an impact on the valuation of the rupee. That is the reason why I am pushing for this. Every 1 per cent depreciation of the rupee has an impact of Rs. 46 billion on Government\u2019s expenditure. That is the concern. One per cent interest rate has an impact of Rs.160 billion on the economy. So, Hon. Minister, we do not need to tell you these things because you have practical knowledge. Therefore, what I am saying is, together, we must ensure that the economy does not get stymied or get caught to the bureaucratic forces who are out there.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) I am not debating, Sir. I am only trying to ensure that Sri Lanka - [Interruption.]\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0db1\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0bc8\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) Hon. Member, thank you very much for the points made. Of course, the Central Bank would take into account all those points.\n\nThen, with regard to the swap we have with the People\u2019s Bank of China, I would say that it is not a new thing; it has been there all this time. - [Interruption.] That is true, but the target is to build up the NIR, and the Central Bank will manage these things."
  },
