    "chunk_text": "\u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dba\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dba\u0dca\u0db6 \u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dc1\u0dba \u0b85 \u0b9a \u0baa\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb4\u0b95 \u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd \u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0bae\u0b9f\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0baf\u0bb1\u0bb2\u0bcd: \u0baa\u0bbf \u0ba4\u0bc8 \u0b85\u0bae\u0bc8\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbf, \u0b89\u0baf\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0bc8\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd\n\n\u0ba4\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb4\u0bbf\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bae\u0bc8\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bb5\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0ba4\u0bc1\n\n\u0b95\u0bc2\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\n\nBRAIN DRAIN OF GRADUATES OF STATE UNIVERSITIES: STATEMENT BY PRIME MINISTER\n\nAND MINISTER OF EDUCATION, HIGHER EDUCATION AND VOCATIONAL EDUCATION\n\n1. Details of public university graduates who have left the country within one year of graduation are not available. 2. There is no restriction imposed on graduates who passed out from State universities with regard to serving in other countries. Therefore, calculation of the expenditure as a percentage of GDP is not required.\n\n3. There are no contractual agreements between graduates and the Government in terms of their departing the country after graduation.\n\n4. Taxes, as you know, are collected by the Government mainly from two sources, as direct taxes and indirect taxes. All taxes are contributed towards maintaining the free education system in the country and it is done with the intention of providing all students an equal opportunity to access quality education irrespective of their socio-economic background. There are no restrictions placed on those graduates about how they may use their knowledge, either in the country or outside the country.\n\n5. The Government has not imposed any regulations or any kind of obligation on students who receive Mahapola Fund or free education about serving the country for a minimum period.\n\n6. No such proposal has been introduced by the Government to recover money spent as expenses on an individual graduate, if they go abroad and find employment.\n\n7. The Government has not taken any policy decision to recover money spent by the Government on free education of the students."
  },
